    heading: "What a Telr integration costs to build",
    note: `If a maintained plugin fits your cart and your checkout is standard, this is a small job and we will quote it as one: install, configure, harden, test, document. If you are building a new store, Telr checkout is included in the store price from ${P.shop}. Adding Telr to an existing custom site is quoted after we read the code, because the cost lives in how your current order states are written rather than in the gateway calls. Subscriptions, customer portals with saved cards and two-provider setups are custom work from ${P.software}, and in-app checkout inside a new app starts from ${P.app}. Telr's own charges, whatever they are for your business, are paid to Telr and never pass through our invoice; see <a href='/pricing/'>our pricing</a> for the build side.`,
